  "english": "CANON OF THE COMING OF THE HOLY SPIRIT\n\nOn the Sunday of the Coming of the Holy Spirit, which is called Pentecost, that is, the fiftieth day from Pascha. \nAt night there is a vigil, and they shall place the Holy Sacrament upon the table of preparation. \nProcessional hymn (tone [gd]): \"Our Lord ascended into heaven\" (Hambartsaw tērn mer yerkins). \nHymn of blessing [ah.] Tone 4 [dz]: \"The dove-like apostle\" (Arakeloy aghawnwoy). \nFirst Alleluia: \"A clean heart...\" \"Cast me not...\" \nResponse: \"The wings of a dove covered with silver...\" \"When the heavenly King scattered...\" \nHymn of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 1 [ah]: \"The Coming of the Spirit\" (Hogwoyn zgaloustn), with its variables. \nMorning Song: \"Let us bless the Coming of the Spirit\" (Zgaloust hogwoyn orhnescouk), \"Bless the Lord in the churches\" (Yekegeghetsis orhnetsek). \nLitany: \"Let us all say\" (Asascouk amen). \n\"Holy God,\" who didst come and rest in the apostles. \nDuring this week, this Song, Litany, and \"Holy God\" are used. \nAnd they shall go out in procession with the Cross and the Gospel and with all adornments, singing the hymn, Tone 4 [dz]: \"The dove-like apostle\" (Arakeloy aghawnwoy). \nThen Psalm 142 [143]. \nAntiphon: \"Thy good and holy Spirit.\" \nResponse: \"Lord, hear my prayer.\" \nActs 2:1: \"And when the day... [to verse 21]... the Lord shall be saved.\" \nAlleluia, Psalm 142 [143]: \"Thy good and holy Spirit.\" \nGospel according to John 14:15: \"If you love me... [to verse 24]... who sent me.\" \nLitany: \"For the peace from above\" (Vasn i veroust). \nAnd they shall sign the four corners of the world with the Cross [Andastan]. \nLitany: \"By the Holy Cross\" (Sourb khachivs). \nPrayer: \"Guardian\" (Pahpanea). \nAnd then they shall begin the hymn of rest in the proper tone. \nPsalm 129 [130]: \"Let thine ears...\" \nResponse: \"Out of the depths.\" \nGospel according to Luke 12:49: \"I am come to send fire... [to verse 59]... the very last mite.\" \nThen \"Spirit of Souls\" (Hogots). \nLitany: \"For the souls of them that are asleep\" (Vasn hangoutseal). \nPrayer: \"Christ, Son of God.\" \nAnd then the hymn, Tone 2 [be]: \"Indivisible Trinity\" (Yerrordoutiun anbazhaneli). \nThen \"Newly-created\" (Norasteghtseal). \nLitany: \"Let us ask\" (Khndrescouk), \"Save us\" (Ketso). \nPrayer: \"To Thy all-powerful and wondrous coming, O Holy Spirit and God, we bow down.\" \nMidday Introit: \"We confess Thee, O God\" (Astouats zkez khostovanimk). \nPsalm: \"The Lord reigneth.\" \nHymn, Tone 2 [by]: \"Who from the ever-moving\" (Or i harasharzh). \nPsalm 148: \"Praise the Lord from the heavens,\" \"Praise the Lord with a song,\" \"Praise God,\" \"I was small.\" \nActs 2:1: \"And when the day... [to verse 21]... the Lord shall be saved.\" \nAlleluia, Psalm 32 [33]: \"By the mercy of the Lord.\" \nGospel according to John 14:25: \"These things have I spoken unto you... [to verse 31]... let us go hence.\" \nEucharistic Hymn [Serbasatsoutiun]: \"Angelic\" (Hreshtakayin). \nBut when the celebrant reaches that place where he says: \"Take, eat,\" the clerks shall sing the hymn, Tone 2 [by]: \"Awesome wind\" (Sarsapeli hoghmoy). \nPrayer with kneeling: \"Let us pray to the Lord\" (Ztēr aghachesgouk), three times. \nThen: \"And again in peace.\" \n\"Blessing and glory.\" \nAnd then they shall read the three Prayers of Saint John Chrysostom, which were spoken to the Holy Trinity: \"Almighty, undefiled God.\" \nAnd at the completion: \"Heavenly Father\" (Hayr yerk). \nHymn, Tone 2 [bk]: \"Today the heavenly hosts\" (Aysor yerknayinkn). \nPrayer with kneeling",
